J5 roll      wrist_roll       vs wrist_rotator      -90.00 deg.. 90.00  gap   0.00 mm to servo_SG90             hit      6.0 mm3  control     13.0 mm3 at 1 pitches

positive control fired at all 1 stations: each moving part was driven along its own MEASURED closing vector, past contact, and the sampler saw it. The check can see.
  HOW DEEP EACH ONE HAD TO GO, in sample pitches. This is the gate's resolution
  at that station, and it qualifies the clear rows above: a joint whose
  control only fires 4 pitches in is a joint where a sliver 3 pitches thick
  would have gone unseen, so its clear is a weaker clear.
    J5 roll      1 pitches (1.00 mm past contact) ->     13.0 mm3

WEAKER THAN THE REST, and named rather than averaged in:
  J5 roll: the 6.0 mm3 against the motor is the DESIGNED PRESS FIT, not a strike. This is the one station whose moving part IS the part bored onto the spline, so the interference the broach exists to create is inside the swept volume: an Oe4.65 bore on an Oe4.90 spline over 2.50 mm is 4.7 mm3 of annulus by arithmetic, and the sampler sees 6.0. It also does not vary across the sweep, which is the tell - a strike that is the same at every angle is a seating condition, not a collision.

